                                "sense_id": "c3f2a84a-9cba-330d-988e-7739499502dc",
                                "text": "Mind, by being modelled in men's imaginations into a Shape, a Visibility ; and reasoned of as if it had been some composite, divisible and reunitable substance, some finer chemical salt, or curious piece of logical joinery, — began to lose its immaterial, mysterious, divine though invisible character: it was tacitly figured as something that might, were our organs fine enough, be seen."
